WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.890
27 March 2014.

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:07.630
The UN General Assembly votes on a
resolution called Territorial integrity of

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:08.440
Ukraine.

4
00:00:08.490 --> 00:00:13.030
100 for, 11 against, 58 abstentions.

5
00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.330
It underscores the invalidity of
the 16 March referendum in Crimea.

6
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.410
2 March 2022.

7
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:23.630
A second resolution,
Aggression against Ukraine,

8
00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:28.130
passes 141 to 5, with 35 abstaining.

9
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.950
It demands that Russia unconditionally
withdraw all of its military forces.

10
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.530
Two votes, two majorities.

11
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.770
So why couldn't the votes
protect Ukraine's borders?

12
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.910
In this mission, you'll pin down
sovereignty and territorial integrity,

13
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.970
and map how Ukraine's
population mix varied by region.

14
00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.710
Then you'll weigh the challenges
to Ukraine's government,

15
00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.350
from contested territory
to a shrinking economy.

16
00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:58.280
Your mission: explain why UN majorities
could not protect Ukraine's borders.
